WEBVTT

00:04.371 --> 00:07.037
(liquid squirting rhythmically)

00:21.454 --> 00:23.538
(flies buzzing)

00:25.579 --> 00:27.705
(squirting continuing)

00:33.454 --> 00:35.037
Soldier:
It's time to go.

00:37.037 --> 00:38.996
Did you hear me?

00:39.079 --> 00:42.538
This is an evacuation.
You understand?

00:42.621 --> 00:44.329
You have to come with me.

00:44.413 --> 00:46.162
Why?

00:46.246 --> 00:49.329
Because they told me,
so now I'm telling you.

00:49.413 --> 00:51.913
Everyone in this
village, everyone.

00:51.996 --> 00:53.913
It's not safe here.
There's radiation
in the air.

00:53.996 --> 00:55.955
What's wrong with you?

00:56.037 --> 00:57.621
Do you know how old I am?

00:57.705 --> 00:59.246
(flies buzzing)

00:59.329 --> 01:01.871
I don't know. Old.

01:01.955 --> 01:04.329
I'm 82.

01:04.413 --> 01:06.746
I've lived here my whole life.

01:06.830 --> 01:10.162
Right here, that house,
this place.

01:10.246 --> 01:14.162
Old Woman:
What do I care about safe?

01:14.246 --> 01:18.162
Soldier:
I have a job.
Don't cause trouble.

01:18.246 --> 01:19.621
Old Woman:
Trouble?

01:19.705 --> 01:23.705
You're not the first soldier
to stand here with a gun.

01:23.788 --> 01:26.830
When I was 12,
the revolution came.

01:26.913 --> 01:31.037
Czar's men.
Then Bolsheviks.

01:31.121 --> 01:33.955
Boys like you
marching in lines.

01:34.037 --> 01:37.287
They told us to leave. No.

01:37.371 --> 01:39.871
Then there was Stalin
and his famine,

01:39.955 --> 01:42.037
the Holodomor.

01:42.121 --> 01:46.162
My parents died.
Two of my sisters died.

01:46.246 --> 01:48.871
They told the rest of us
to leave.

01:48.955 --> 01:50.538
No.

01:50.621 --> 01:52.371
Then the Great War.

01:52.454 --> 01:55.663
German boys.
Russian boys.

01:55.746 --> 01:59.287
More soldiers,
more famine, more bodies.

02:00.287 --> 02:03.037
My brothers
never came home.

02:03.121 --> 02:06.663
But I stayed,
and I'm still here.

02:06.746 --> 02:09.913
After all that I have seen...

02:09.996 --> 02:12.079
so I should leave now,

02:12.162 --> 02:15.746
because of something
I cannot see at all?

02:15.830 --> 02:16.788
No.

02:16.871 --> 02:18.996
(squirting continuing)

02:21.246 --> 02:23.287
-(bucket clanking)
-(milk swishing)

02:30.329 --> 02:34.329
-(horn honking)
-Just one moment!

02:41.830 --> 02:44.913
-(clanks)
-It's time to go.

02:51.621 --> 02:53.830
(sighs)
Please stand up now.

02:53.913 --> 02:56.037
(rhythmic squirting)

02:57.204 --> 02:59.329
(flies buzzing)

03:02.705 --> 03:04.287
(gun cocks)

03:04.371 --> 03:06.162
This is your
last warning.

03:12.705 --> 03:15.830
-(gunshot)
-(body thuds)

03:22.996 --> 03:24.871
It's time to go.

03:33.413 --> 03:35.538
(flies buzzing)

04:12.871 --> 04:14.955
(leaves rustling)

04:29.454 --> 04:31.579
(locks clanking)

04:37.913 --> 04:39.454
Woman:
Come on.

05:38.037 --> 05:41.413
(dosimeters clicking)

05:43.496 --> 05:45.705
Soldier (muffled):
Point four.

05:56.371 --> 05:58.204
Soldier 2:
Point six.

06:02.579 --> 06:05.204
-(dosimeter crackling)
-Soldier 3: Fifteen.

06:08.579 --> 06:10.705
(dosimeter crackling)

06:22.037 --> 06:25.746
(helicopter whirring overhead)

06:46.037 --> 06:48.204
(distant helicopters whirring)

06:57.496 --> 06:59.454
(phone rings)

07:02.454 --> 07:03.579
Legasov.

07:03.663 --> 07:05.871
(man speaking indistinctly
over phone)

07:05.955 --> 07:07.621
I'll meet him there.

07:19.746 --> 07:21.830
(trucks rumbling)

08:06.329 --> 08:08.538
Legasov:
The atom is a humbling thing.

08:09.996 --> 08:12.830
It's not humbling,
it's humiliating.

08:14.746 --> 08:16.413
Why is the core still
exposed to the air?

08:16.496 --> 08:18.454
Why have we not
already covered it up?

08:18.538 --> 08:22.413
We want to,
but we can't get close enough.

08:22.496 --> 08:26.329
The debris on the roof is
graphite from the core itself.

08:26.413 --> 08:30.496
Until we can push it off
the roof back into the reactor,

08:30.579 --> 08:32.788
it'll kill anyone
who gets near it.

08:32.871 --> 08:37.246
You can see the roof
is in three levels.

08:37.329 --> 08:40.496
We've named them--
the small one here is Katya.

08:40.579 --> 08:42.705
One thousand roentgen per hour.

08:42.788 --> 08:45.705
Presume two hours
of exposure is fatal.

08:45.788 --> 08:47.454
The one on the side-- Nina.

08:47.538 --> 08:49.663
Two thousand roentgen.
One hour, fatal.

08:49.746 --> 08:52.913
We used remote-controlled
bulldozers in Afghanistan.

08:52.996 --> 08:56.079
Too heavy.
They'd fall
right through.

08:56.162 --> 08:59.830
-So then...?
-Moon rovers.

08:59.913 --> 09:01.788
Lunokhod STR-1's.
They're light.

09:01.871 --> 09:04.663
And if we line them
with lead, they can
withstand the radiation.

09:04.746 --> 09:06.329
Shcherbina:
We couldn't put
a man on the moon.

09:06.413 --> 09:09.413
At least we can keep
a man off a roof.

09:09.496 --> 09:11.663
That is the most important
thing, General.

09:11.746 --> 09:14.830
Under no circumstances
can men go up there.

09:14.913 --> 09:17.329
Robots only.

09:17.413 --> 09:20.079
What about this
large section here?

09:20.913 --> 09:22.538
Masha.

09:23.496 --> 09:25.413
Twelve thousand roentgen.

09:26.830 --> 09:30.830
If you were to stand there
in full protective gear
head-to-toe for two minutes,

09:30.913 --> 09:32.705
your life expectancy
would be cut in half.

09:32.788 --> 09:35.162
By three minutes,
you're dead within months.

09:35.246 --> 09:38.329
Even our lunar rovers
won't work on Masha.

09:38.413 --> 09:41.830
That amount of gamma radiation
penetrates everything.

09:41.913 --> 09:43.246
The particles
literally shred

09:43.329 --> 09:45.329
the circuits
in microchips apart.

09:45.413 --> 09:48.162
If it's more complicated
than a light switch,

09:48.246 --> 09:49.746
Masha will destroy it.

09:49.830 --> 09:51.246
It would be fair
to say that

09:51.329 --> 09:54.454
that piece of roof is the most
dangerous place on Earth.

10:00.621 --> 10:04.287
So... what do we do?

10:06.287 --> 10:08.579
That's
what we wanted
to ask you.

11:01.705 --> 11:03.830
(indistinct chattering)

11:17.705 --> 11:19.871
(bottles clinking)

11:26.496 --> 11:28.371
(man coughing)

11:41.621 --> 11:44.496
(men singing)

12:25.579 --> 12:27.788
Tent 181?

12:31.162 --> 12:33.621
(scoffs, grunts)

12:42.371 --> 12:43.830
It's all right.
It's free.

12:45.121 --> 12:46.621
It's a little early.

12:50.413 --> 12:51.830
(grunts)

12:59.955 --> 13:01.079
Bacho.

13:03.329 --> 13:04.454
Pavel.

13:05.705 --> 13:07.287
-Yeah?
-Mm.

13:11.788 --> 13:13.663
What unit
were you in?

13:13.746 --> 13:16.079
Uh, they had me
in motor pool in Kiev,

13:16.162 --> 13:18.913
-but then they--
-Not this bullshit.

13:18.996 --> 13:20.329
In Afghanistan.

13:20.413 --> 13:23.621
Oh, um, I wasn't
in Afghanistan.

13:26.246 --> 13:27.538
I'm not in the military.

13:29.788 --> 13:32.538
(sighs)
They're running
out of men.

13:38.329 --> 13:40.454
(indistinct chattering)

13:44.538 --> 13:46.246
Showers. Food.

13:46.329 --> 13:49.037
Those guys,
they dig up the ground.

13:49.121 --> 13:51.621
Those guys,
they cut down trees.

13:51.705 --> 13:55.162
Those guys, they evacuate
people, I think,

13:55.246 --> 13:56.705
like villagers.

13:58.162 --> 13:59.246
What about them?

14:00.371 --> 14:02.246
I don't know them.
Fuck them.

14:04.496 --> 14:05.579
Janek!

14:07.079 --> 14:09.579
-What do you want?
-Give me an egg basket.

14:09.663 --> 14:12.913
-No, I've only got the one--
-Give me the fucking basket!

14:16.371 --> 14:18.788
He's with me,
you understand?

14:18.871 --> 14:20.538
Nobody fucks with him.

14:22.996 --> 14:24.830
We make these
from lead scrap.

14:24.913 --> 14:27.162
-Put it on
under your balls.
-Now?

14:27.246 --> 14:30.079
No, no. You can wait until
the radiation gives you a cunt.

14:30.162 --> 14:31.830
Yes, now.

14:33.955 --> 14:36.871
Over your clothes.
Fucking shit.

14:45.121 --> 14:47.538
-You ever go hunting?
-No.

14:48.371 --> 14:51.621
Well... today's
your lucky day.

14:51.705 --> 14:54.079
You, me,

14:54.162 --> 14:57.955
that ugly Armenian
in the tent, Garo,
we do animal control.

14:59.329 --> 15:00.705
Animal control?

15:00.788 --> 15:02.788
Yeah, they're
radioactive,

15:02.871 --> 15:05.121
so they have to go.

15:05.204 --> 15:07.413
But it's not hard.
They're mostly pets.

15:07.496 --> 15:10.955
They're happy to see you.
They run right up to you.

15:11.037 --> 15:11.996
Bang!

15:12.079 --> 15:13.538
You load the bodies
on the truck,

15:13.621 --> 15:15.996
dump them in a pit,
bury them in concrete.

15:16.079 --> 15:17.788
And then we drink.

15:17.871 --> 15:22.121
As much vodka as you want,
plus a thousand rubles.

15:24.496 --> 15:25.996
Let's go get you a gun.

15:54.329 --> 15:55.913
(gate buzzes)

16:35.121 --> 16:36.079
Yes?

16:36.162 --> 16:38.246
I need to see
the following documents.

16:38.329 --> 16:40.162
They're listed
as permission only.

16:46.454 --> 16:48.663
I'm working for
the Central Committee.

17:00.538 --> 17:01.913
Comrade?

17:06.955 --> 17:08.663
(door opens)

17:21.579 --> 17:22.621
(door closes)

17:34.996 --> 17:36.454
(door opens)

17:40.079 --> 17:41.746
Agent:
She can have that one.

17:50.413 --> 17:52.246
Thank you, Comrade.

17:55.746 --> 17:57.871
(engines rumbling)

18:11.871 --> 18:13.996
(helicopters whirring)

18:35.830 --> 18:39.121
(muffled breathing)

19:24.204 --> 19:26.371
(voices murmuring)

19:30.287 --> 19:31.621
Man (over walkie-talkie):
All clear.

19:31.705 --> 19:34.121
Tarakanov:
Bring up the cameras.

19:34.204 --> 19:36.037
(buzzing)

19:38.204 --> 19:40.287
-Tarakanov: Signal?
-Jughashvili: Acceptable.

19:40.371 --> 19:42.287
Running onboard diagnostics.

19:42.371 --> 19:44.204
Tarakonov:
Tell me when we're
ready to move it.

19:44.287 --> 19:47.538
To think that's what
we put on the moon.

19:49.871 --> 19:51.579
Well, not that one.

19:53.371 --> 19:54.955
I know not that one.

19:55.037 --> 19:58.538
This rover was in storage.
They can build two more.

19:58.621 --> 20:00.913
That should cover
Nina and Katya.

20:01.871 --> 20:03.121
Shcherbina:
And Masha?

20:03.204 --> 20:05.287
Tarakanov:
The Central Committee
have informed me

20:05.371 --> 20:06.830
that they may have
found something

20:06.913 --> 20:09.496
that could work up there.
From the outside.

20:09.579 --> 20:11.287
American?

20:11.371 --> 20:13.287
(chuckling):
Of course not.

20:13.371 --> 20:15.079
It's a German
police robot.

20:15.162 --> 20:17.579
West German, so,
as you can imagine,

20:17.663 --> 20:20.037
that wasn't an easy
conversation to have.

20:20.121 --> 20:21.329
Diagnostics complete.

20:21.413 --> 20:23.913
Ready to engage
main power and motor.

20:24.579 --> 20:25.871
Tarakanov:
Begin.

20:31.913 --> 20:33.413
Can we move it?

20:35.121 --> 20:36.538
(controller clicks)

20:46.246 --> 20:49.079
Valery, what's that?
A smile?

20:50.621 --> 20:52.413
(Shcherbina laughing)

20:52.496 --> 20:54.663
(helicopters whirring outside)

21:02.538 --> 21:03.705
(knock at door)

21:03.788 --> 21:05.913
(door opens, closes)

21:08.204 --> 21:10.830
Khomyuk:
I see your condition has
improved, Comrade Dyatlov.

21:10.913 --> 21:12.454
No. Leave.

21:20.371 --> 21:22.579
I need your help.

21:30.037 --> 21:33.413
Akimov initiated AZ-5.

21:33.496 --> 21:36.204
-When you gave the order--
-Order? What order?

21:37.788 --> 21:40.955
Toptunov called it out,
Akimov pressed it.

21:41.996 --> 21:43.621
It was the only good
decision they made.

21:43.705 --> 21:45.287
Incompetent morons.

21:46.162 --> 21:49.204
Can you confirm that
the reactor exploded

21:49.287 --> 21:51.121
after they attempted
to shut it down?

21:52.121 --> 21:54.496
How do I even know
it exploded, huh?

21:59.121 --> 22:01.204
(papers rustling)

22:15.454 --> 22:18.037
I found this
in the state archive.

22:18.913 --> 22:20.955
Written in 1976.

22:21.037 --> 22:24.955
It's about the operation
of RBMK reactors
under extreme conditions.

22:25.037 --> 22:26.579
So?

22:26.663 --> 22:29.037
The names of the authors
have been redacted,

22:29.121 --> 22:31.246
and two pages
have been removed.

22:31.913 --> 22:35.287
Well, the State must protect
its secrets, Comrade.

22:35.371 --> 22:37.830
Do you dare
suggest otherwise?

22:37.913 --> 22:40.246
They made a mistake.

22:41.788 --> 22:44.913
They didn't redact
the table of contents.

22:55.871 --> 22:57.371
The missing pages
apparently refer

22:57.454 --> 23:01.371
to a positive void
coefficient and AZ-5.

23:02.287 --> 23:03.663
Does that mean
anything to you?

23:03.746 --> 23:06.162
What are you after here?
Why are you asking me this?

23:06.246 --> 23:08.538
You worked with the reactor.
You know it better than I do.

23:08.621 --> 23:11.705
So everything's
my fault, then?

23:11.788 --> 23:12.830
Is that what this is?

23:12.913 --> 23:14.413
I'm not here
to blame you.

23:14.496 --> 23:16.996
I'm here to find out
what happened.

23:17.079 --> 23:18.413
And whether you
realize it or not,

23:18.496 --> 23:20.746
I'm your best chance
to avoid a bullet.

23:23.413 --> 23:25.204
Can you help me or not?

23:33.579 --> 23:36.037
I have no idea what
would've gone here.

23:36.121 --> 23:39.162
Void coefficients have
nothing to do with AZ-5.

23:40.079 --> 23:42.079
There.
Now you can go.

23:42.162 --> 23:44.955
-You're not even curious?
-What for?

23:46.121 --> 23:49.454
You think the right question
will get you the truth? (scoffs)

23:50.621 --> 23:52.746
There is no truth.

23:52.830 --> 23:56.705
Ask the bosses
whatever you want
and you'll get the lie.

23:56.788 --> 23:59.121
And I will get the bullet.

24:03.955 --> 24:06.287
(door opens, closes)

24:14.788 --> 24:16.955
(truck rumbling)

25:09.496 --> 25:11.913
(rifle clicking)

25:32.204 --> 25:34.246
I only have two rules.

25:34.329 --> 25:35.871
One.

25:35.955 --> 25:38.955
Don't point this gun at me.
That's easy, right?

25:39.037 --> 25:40.955
You can point it
at this piece of shit.

25:41.037 --> 25:43.162
I don't give a fuck.
Never me.

25:43.246 --> 25:45.037
Two.

25:45.121 --> 25:48.496
If you hit an animal
and it doesn't die,

25:48.579 --> 25:51.287
keep shooting
until it does.

25:51.371 --> 25:55.371
Don't let them suffer,
or I'll kill you.

25:55.454 --> 25:57.663
Understand?

25:57.746 --> 25:59.079
I mean it.

26:00.079 --> 26:02.037
I've killed a lot of people.

26:07.037 --> 26:09.621
Good.
Then we're ready.

26:49.079 --> 26:52.579
Once we start, they'll run
inside where they feel safe.

26:52.663 --> 26:54.746
So we go
door-to-door.

26:55.996 --> 26:57.371
Okay?

26:57.454 --> 26:58.955
Good.

27:01.204 --> 27:03.329
(whistling)

27:05.162 --> 27:07.913
(distant dog barking)

27:07.996 --> 27:09.705
(panting)

27:12.913 --> 27:15.121
(whistling continues)

27:30.746 --> 27:32.454
-(gunshots echo)
-(dog yelps)

27:33.913 --> 27:35.705
(gunshots echoing)

27:37.996 --> 27:39.371
(panting)

27:40.746 --> 27:42.538
-(gunshot echoes)
-(dog whimpers)

27:49.079 --> 27:49.996
Hey!

27:50.079 --> 27:53.037
Do your job.
Door-to-door.

27:54.246 --> 27:55.996
(distant dogs barking)

28:09.162 --> 28:12.246
-(gunshots echoing)
-(dog barking)

28:30.746 --> 28:32.204
(distant gunshot echoes)

28:36.162 --> 28:38.496
(dog panting)

28:38.579 --> 28:39.663
(distant gunshot echoes)

28:39.746 --> 28:41.454
(panting)

28:46.871 --> 28:49.037
(muttering):
Go. Go.

28:49.121 --> 28:51.579
Go away. Go!

28:55.621 --> 28:57.746
(panting)

28:59.413 --> 29:01.746
-(barks)
-(gunshot echoes)

29:03.287 --> 29:05.121
(dog whimpering)

29:13.538 --> 29:15.287
(dog whimpering)

29:16.955 --> 29:18.329
(distant gunshot echoes)

29:21.996 --> 29:25.246
(dog panting, whimpering)

29:27.246 --> 29:28.955
(panting)

29:34.621 --> 29:35.746
(gunshot echoes)

29:47.579 --> 29:49.413
Don't let them suffer.

29:49.496 --> 29:51.454
Sorry. Sorry.

29:53.496 --> 29:55.996
Bacho:
You're dragging that
to the truck.

30:02.913 --> 30:04.496
(distant gunshot echoes)

30:24.329 --> 30:26.204
(flies buzzing)

30:32.996 --> 30:34.496
You gonna eat?

30:45.204 --> 30:46.538
Drink.

30:50.204 --> 30:51.538
Again.

31:03.663 --> 31:04.913
Look...

31:07.371 --> 31:09.705
This happens to everyone
their first time.

31:10.621 --> 31:12.996
Normally when
you kill a man.

31:14.538 --> 31:16.287
But for you, a dog.

31:16.371 --> 31:18.621
So what?
There's no shame in it.

31:20.746 --> 31:23.371
You remember
your first time, Garo?

31:23.454 --> 31:27.079
My first time--
Afghanistan.

31:29.121 --> 31:31.329
We were moving
through a house,

31:31.413 --> 31:35.413
and suddenly a man was there
and I shot him in the stomach.

31:37.204 --> 31:39.371
Yeah, that's
a real war story.

31:40.579 --> 31:42.788
They're never any good stories
like in the movies.

31:42.871 --> 31:44.454
They're shit.

31:45.121 --> 31:48.579
A man was there--
boom, stomach.

31:51.079 --> 31:53.037
I was so scared, I didn't
pull the trigger again

31:53.121 --> 31:54.913
for the rest of the day.

31:56.996 --> 31:59.955
I thought,
"Well, that's it, Bacho.

32:01.287 --> 32:03.538
"You put a bullet
in someone.

32:03.621 --> 32:05.871
"You're not you anymore.

32:05.955 --> 32:07.913
You'll never be you again."

32:10.454 --> 32:12.204
But then you wake up
the next morning,

32:12.287 --> 32:14.162
and you're still you.

32:15.246 --> 32:16.830
And you realize...

32:18.121 --> 32:20.579
that was you all along.

32:20.663 --> 32:22.496
You just didn't know.

32:32.913 --> 32:35.496
The happiness of all mankind.

32:39.121 --> 32:40.663
What?

32:41.788 --> 32:45.871
"Our goal is the happiness
of all mankind."

32:45.955 --> 32:47.329
(spits)

32:52.579 --> 32:53.830
Bacho:
Yeah.

32:58.621 --> 33:00.162
I'm happy.

33:00.246 --> 33:01.955
I'm happy every day.

33:04.329 --> 33:07.329
All right.
Back to work.

33:08.830 --> 33:10.121
Come on.

33:24.204 --> 33:27.246
(helicopters whirring overhead)

33:31.538 --> 33:33.746
(debris clattering)

33:50.371 --> 33:52.579
(helicopter whirring)

34:14.663 --> 34:17.079
(controllers clicking)

34:28.454 --> 34:29.788
Tarakanov:
It's here.

34:36.830 --> 34:38.913
(trucks rumbling)

34:58.579 --> 35:00.621
All right.

35:01.955 --> 35:03.329
Get over.

35:03.413 --> 35:05.496
Right. Hang on.

35:06.371 --> 35:08.413
Easy now. Careful.

35:09.121 --> 35:10.621
Hold it!

35:18.454 --> 35:19.746
Joker.

35:21.287 --> 35:23.871
It's what the Germans
named it: "Joker."

35:23.996 --> 35:26.996
-Is it ready?
-It's ready.

35:36.162 --> 35:38.329
(helicopter whirring)

35:53.830 --> 35:55.996
(clanking)

36:07.204 --> 36:09.246
(clicking)

36:14.204 --> 36:16.079
Jughashvili:
Good signal.

36:16.579 --> 36:18.162
Tarakanov:
Cameras.

36:19.413 --> 36:20.913
Motors.

36:22.538 --> 36:25.871
Motors, good.
Signals, good.

36:25.955 --> 36:28.496
All right,
let's take this easy.

36:28.579 --> 36:30.871
Forward one meter,
reverse one meter.

36:33.121 --> 36:34.413
Forward one.

36:38.371 --> 36:39.830
Germans.

36:41.287 --> 36:42.705
Reverse one.

36:48.996 --> 36:51.079
(buttons clacking)

36:56.037 --> 36:58.037
Did you lose the signal?

37:02.579 --> 37:04.579
It's not the signal.
It's the vehicle.

37:06.246 --> 37:07.705
It's dead.

37:13.705 --> 37:14.746
Shit.

37:19.538 --> 37:21.329
Of course I know
they're listening!

37:21.413 --> 37:23.496
I want them to hear!
I want them to hear it all!

37:23.579 --> 37:25.329
Shcherbina:
Do you know
what we're doing here?!

37:25.413 --> 37:28.079
Tell those geniuses
what they have done!

37:29.871 --> 37:31.955
Shcherbina:
I don't give a fuck!

37:33.830 --> 37:35.830
Tell them! Go tell them!
Ryzhkov!

37:35.913 --> 37:37.371
Go tell them he's a joke!

37:37.454 --> 37:39.037
Tell fucking Gorbachev!

37:39.121 --> 37:42.121
-Tell them!
-(phone jangling)

37:52.663 --> 37:54.788
(phone clanking)

38:03.371 --> 38:06.538
The official position
of the State

38:06.621 --> 38:08.830
is that a global
nuclear catastrophe

38:08.913 --> 38:11.246
is not possible
in the Soviet Union.

38:11.329 --> 38:15.871
They told the Germans
that the highest detected
level of radiation

38:15.955 --> 38:18.329
was 2,000 roentgen.

38:18.996 --> 38:21.329
They gave them
the propaganda number.

38:23.746 --> 38:26.121
That robot was
never going to work.

38:30.329 --> 38:31.996
We need a new phone.

38:47.454 --> 38:49.538
(rain pattering)

39:13.538 --> 39:15.496
What if we don't clear it?

39:15.579 --> 39:17.579
We have to clear it.

39:17.663 --> 39:21.663
Legasov:
If we don't clear the roof,
we can't build a cover over it.

39:23.579 --> 39:26.329
If we can't cover it,
that's 12,000 roentgen.

39:26.413 --> 39:30.830
That's nearly twice
the radiation from
the Hiroshima bomb.

39:30.913 --> 39:35.204
-Every hour, hour after--
-Shcherbina: I know,
I know, I know.

39:35.287 --> 39:37.246
What about lead?

39:38.579 --> 39:39.996
We could-- I don't know.

39:40.079 --> 39:43.162
We could melt it
and pour it from above,
like a coating.

39:43.246 --> 39:46.246
Tarakanov: First of all,
we've already used
most of the lead we had--

39:46.329 --> 39:48.496
There's lead sheeting
around the instruments

39:48.579 --> 39:50.287
in the other
reactor buildings.

39:50.371 --> 39:53.246
The soldiers are stripping
it for their armor.

39:53.329 --> 39:55.079
Are you serious?

39:56.746 --> 39:59.788
(scoffs) Even if,
we're still talking about

39:59.871 --> 40:01.913
boiling metal
in a helicopter.

40:01.996 --> 40:04.621
And it's lead, Boris,
it'll weight a ton.

40:07.037 --> 40:10.037
What if we shoot
the graphite into the hole?

40:10.121 --> 40:12.996
We've got high-caliber bullets,
exploding bullets.

40:13.079 --> 40:15.287
-They wouldn't just
ricochet, they'd push--
-(Shcherbina scoffs)

40:15.371 --> 40:17.705
You wanna shoot
exploding bullets

40:17.788 --> 40:19.621
at an exposed
nuclear reactor?

40:19.705 --> 40:21.871
-Well...
-No, no.

40:21.955 --> 40:23.621
Let's go light that roof
back on fire.

40:23.705 --> 40:26.955
It was so easy
to put out the first time.

40:27.037 --> 40:30.579
(sighs)
What are
we talking about here?

40:32.162 --> 40:34.246
We need another robot.

40:35.121 --> 40:37.913
One that can withstand
the radiation.

40:37.996 --> 40:40.454
I've asked.
There is nothing.

40:41.788 --> 40:43.454
The Americans?

40:43.538 --> 40:45.413
If the Americans had
that kind of technology,

40:45.496 --> 40:47.287
do you really think
they'd give it to us?

40:47.371 --> 40:50.329
And even if they would,
the Central Committee
will never stoop to ask.

40:50.413 --> 40:52.121
You know it,
I know it.

40:53.246 --> 40:55.121
There are no robots.

41:01.579 --> 41:03.913
Legasov:
Biorobots.

41:03.996 --> 41:05.663
What was that?

41:07.037 --> 41:08.329
(clears throat)

41:10.162 --> 41:13.788
We use biorobots.

41:16.496 --> 41:17.871
Men.

41:33.996 --> 41:36.162
(distant gunshots echoing)

41:42.955 --> 41:45.037
(dog barking)

41:50.371 --> 41:52.413
(gunshot echoes)

41:56.788 --> 41:58.871
(dog barking)

42:02.204 --> 42:03.538
(distant gunshot echoes)

42:06.037 --> 42:07.371
(gunshot echoes)

42:13.329 --> 42:15.413
(dog growling)

42:18.371 --> 42:19.496
-(gunshot)
-(dog yelps)

42:19.579 --> 42:21.246
(dog whimpering)

42:23.454 --> 42:24.746
(gunshot echoes)

42:46.329 --> 42:47.746
A lot today.

42:52.913 --> 42:55.079
Where do they get their food?

42:57.079 --> 42:58.955
Bacho:
They eat the chickens.

42:59.621 --> 43:01.579
Then they eat each other.

43:12.371 --> 43:13.955
Door-to-door.

44:01.329 --> 44:03.454
(puppy yelps)

44:21.579 --> 44:24.663
(puppies growling, whining)

44:26.079 --> 44:28.204
Bacho:
Pavel?

44:32.496 --> 44:34.121
Bacho:
Pavel!

44:34.204 --> 44:36.371
(footsteps ascending stairs)

44:42.371 --> 44:45.538
You don't hear me?
I'm talking to you.

44:47.579 --> 44:49.162
Fuck.

44:53.955 --> 44:55.746
Just go outside.

44:55.830 --> 44:58.871
(puppies whining, growling)

45:02.204 --> 45:03.579
Go.

45:07.204 --> 45:09.371
(puppies barking)

45:26.538 --> 45:28.579
(exhales)

45:34.663 --> 45:38.246
-(gunshots echoing)
-(sighs)

46:00.788 --> 46:02.913
(gunshots continue)

46:34.955 --> 46:38.287
(man singing
somber Russian song)

46:59.496 --> 47:02.204
(somber song continuing)

47:21.329 --> 47:25.037
(song continuing)

47:43.538 --> 47:45.663
(song fades)

47:51.454 --> 47:53.538
(truck rumbling)

47:57.037 --> 47:58.705
Tarakanov:
Comrade soldiers,

47:58.788 --> 48:01.496
the Soviet people have had
enough of this accident.

48:01.579 --> 48:03.162
They want us to clean this up,

48:03.246 --> 48:05.913
and we have entrusted you
with this serious task.

48:05.996 --> 48:08.287
Because of the nature
of the working area,

48:08.371 --> 48:12.329
you will each have
no more than 90 seconds
to solve this problem.

48:12.413 --> 48:15.287
Listen carefully to each
of my instructions,

48:15.371 --> 48:17.830
and do exactly as
you have been told.

48:17.913 --> 48:22.579
This is for your
own safety and the safety
of your comrades.

48:22.663 --> 48:24.955
You will enter
Reactor Building Three,

48:25.037 --> 48:28.788
climb the stairs
but do not immediately
proceed to the roof.

48:28.871 --> 48:30.871
When you get to the top,
wait inside,

48:30.955 --> 48:33.955
behind the entrance
to the roof
and catch your breath.

48:34.037 --> 48:36.579
You will need it
for what comes next.

48:36.663 --> 48:39.705
This is the working area.
We must clear the graphite.

48:39.788 --> 48:43.287
Some of it is in blocks,
weighing approximately
40 to 50 kilograms.

48:43.371 --> 48:45.496
They all must be thrown
over the edge here.

48:45.579 --> 48:49.496
Watch your comrades moving
fast from this opening,

48:49.579 --> 48:51.162
then turning to the left,

48:51.246 --> 48:53.371
and entering the workspace here.

48:53.454 --> 48:55.079
Take care not to stumble.

48:55.162 --> 48:58.663
There's a hole in the roof.
Take care not to fall.

48:58.746 --> 49:03.454
You will need to move quickly,
and you will need
to move carefully.

49:03.538 --> 49:06.079
Do you understand your mission
as I have described it?

49:06.162 --> 49:08.037
Soldiers:
Yes, Comrade General.

49:08.121 --> 49:11.538
Tarakanov:
These are the most important
90 of your lives.

49:11.621 --> 49:15.037
Commit your task to memory,
then do your job.

49:21.079 --> 49:23.871
(dosimeters clicking)

49:39.329 --> 49:42.121
(metal clanging)

49:58.037 --> 50:00.955
It's time to go.
After 90 seconds,
I will ring a bell.

50:01.037 --> 50:03.162
When you hear it,
return immediately,

50:03.246 --> 50:04.538
drop your shovels in the bin,

50:04.621 --> 50:07.204
and proceed down the hallway
for decontamination.

50:07.287 --> 50:08.996
Above all,
while on the roof,

50:09.079 --> 50:10.538
throw your debris
over the rail.

50:10.621 --> 50:12.371
Do not look over the rail.
Is that clear?

50:13.705 --> 50:15.079
Very well.

50:15.162 --> 50:17.705
On my mark.
Ready. Go.

50:21.037 --> 50:23.246
-(muffled breathing)
-(dosimeters clicking)

50:26.996 --> 50:29.079
(muffled panting)

50:41.996 --> 50:44.955
(clicking grows louder)

50:47.579 --> 50:50.079
(muffled grunting)

50:59.246 --> 51:02.413
(dosimeters crackling loudly)

51:11.204 --> 51:13.079
(grunts)

51:26.454 --> 51:28.579
(both panting)

51:49.538 --> 51:51.621
(alarm clanging)

51:57.121 --> 51:59.079
Whoa!

52:01.955 --> 52:04.204
-(clanging continues)
-(dosimeter crackling)

52:04.287 --> 52:06.788
(panting)

52:06.871 --> 52:08.663
(grunts)

52:10.830 --> 52:12.538
(yelps)

52:23.287 --> 52:25.496
(panting)

52:30.621 --> 52:31.705
Comrade soldier.

52:33.496 --> 52:34.996
You're done.

52:37.454 --> 52:39.538
(dosimeter clicking)

52:46.121 --> 52:48.287
(sighs)
Time to go.

52:48.371 --> 52:50.538
(children chattering)

53:01.204 --> 53:03.663
Oh! Your glove!

53:06.621 --> 53:09.329
(gasps, labored breathing)

53:12.830 --> 53:14.663
(moaning)

53:17.996 --> 53:20.079
(moaning continues)

53:23.538 --> 53:24.996
Mommy! Mommy!

53:39.371 --> 53:41.454
(truck rumbling)

54:29.496 --> 54:31.746
Shcherbina:
I'm sorry for all this.

54:31.830 --> 54:35.496
But we needed to speak
to you somewhere without...

54:35.579 --> 54:38.496
Legasov:
They're going to put
Dyatlov on trial,

54:38.579 --> 54:40.871
and Bryukhanov and Fomin.

54:40.955 --> 54:44.871
We're going to be asked
to give expert testimony,

54:44.955 --> 54:46.454
all three of us.

54:46.538 --> 54:49.037
But that's--
Before that happens--

54:49.121 --> 54:52.579
The Central Committee is
sending Legasov to Vienna.

54:52.663 --> 54:54.621
It's the headquarters
of the International--

54:54.705 --> 54:58.121
Atomic Energy Agency.
Yeah, I know what's in Vienna.

54:59.913 --> 55:01.579
What are they
asking you to do?

55:01.663 --> 55:04.705
Tell the world
what happened.

55:09.329 --> 55:11.663
Well, then you better
know what happened.

55:11.746 --> 55:13.705
I've constructed
a timeline,

55:13.788 --> 55:15.371
minute by minute.

55:15.454 --> 55:18.538
Second by second
in some places.

55:18.621 --> 55:20.413
Every decision,
every button push,

55:20.496 --> 55:22.579
every turn of a switch.

55:22.663 --> 55:25.538
And? Are they guilty?

55:25.621 --> 55:26.996
Yes.

55:27.079 --> 55:31.079
Of gross incompetence,
violation of safety regulations,

55:31.162 --> 55:33.329
recklessness beyond belief.

55:33.413 --> 55:35.996
But the explosion?
I'm not sure.

55:36.079 --> 55:38.413
What do you mean
you're not sure?

55:39.246 --> 55:41.329
I've analyzed the data.

55:41.413 --> 55:43.579
Toptunov was telling the truth.

55:43.663 --> 55:47.037
They shut the reactor down,
and then it exploded.

55:48.454 --> 55:51.830
I think this article
my have the answer,

55:51.913 --> 55:55.371
but two pages
have been removed.

56:00.913 --> 56:02.788
You've seen this before.

56:02.871 --> 56:05.621
Please, believe me
when I tell you that

56:05.705 --> 56:08.121
I had no idea it could
cause an explosion.

56:08.204 --> 56:11.204
-None of us knew.
-None of you knew what?

56:12.496 --> 56:15.496
In 1975, in an RBMK
reactor in Leningrad,

56:15.579 --> 56:17.913
a fuel channel ruptured.

56:17.996 --> 56:19.788
The operators pressed AZ-5,

56:19.871 --> 56:22.621
but instead of the power
going down immediately,

56:22.705 --> 56:25.579
for a brief moment
it went up.

56:25.663 --> 56:27.413
How is that possible?

56:27.496 --> 56:28.871
Well, this was
the very question posed

56:28.955 --> 56:30.871
by a colleague of mine
named Volkov.

56:30.955 --> 56:32.913
He's the one who
wrote this article.

56:32.996 --> 56:36.746
When an RBMK reactor
runs at low power,
it's notoriously unstable.

56:36.830 --> 56:40.162
Prone to swings
in reactivity.

56:40.246 --> 56:41.663
Under normal circumstances,

56:41.746 --> 56:43.579
the control rods can
compensate for that.

56:43.663 --> 56:45.037
Under normal circumstances.

56:45.121 --> 56:48.579
The Chernobyl staff stalled
the reactor during the test.

56:48.663 --> 56:50.496
They pulled almost
all the control rods out

56:50.579 --> 56:54.413
-to bring the power back up.
-This is what Volkov learned
from Leningrad.

56:54.496 --> 56:55.913
If the boron control rods

56:55.996 --> 56:58.705
are completely withdrawn
from the reactor,

56:58.788 --> 57:00.079
when they're put back in,

57:00.162 --> 57:03.287
the first thing that enters
the core isn't boron.

57:03.371 --> 57:05.579
It's graphite.

57:08.746 --> 57:10.996
The control rods
have graphite tips

57:11.079 --> 57:13.496
that displace
water and steam.

57:13.579 --> 57:15.913
So the reactivity
doesn't go down.

57:15.996 --> 57:18.079
It goes up dramatically.

57:18.162 --> 57:21.538
(scoffs)
Why on Earth would
they press that button?

57:21.621 --> 57:23.621
They didn't know.

57:25.454 --> 57:28.079
Legasov:
Volkov warned
the Kremlin,

57:28.162 --> 57:29.913
ten years ago.

57:30.663 --> 57:33.204
(sighs)
But there could
be no doubt

57:33.287 --> 57:37.162
about the supremacy of
the Soviet nuclear industry.

57:37.246 --> 57:39.079
Ah.

57:39.162 --> 57:42.830
The KGB classified it
as a state secret.

57:45.079 --> 57:46.579
Legasov:
When I saw the reactor
blown open,

57:46.663 --> 57:50.121
I still didn't think it could
be this flaw in AZ-5.

57:50.204 --> 57:53.246
Because the flaw will not
lead to an explosion

57:53.329 --> 57:58.496
unless the operators
have pushed the reactor
to the edge of disaster.

57:58.579 --> 58:01.413
-So it is their fault?
-Yes.

58:01.496 --> 58:03.538
But not only
their fault.

58:04.955 --> 58:06.454
No.

58:07.579 --> 58:10.162
Is that what you're
going to say in Vienna?

58:11.871 --> 58:12.996
(sighs)

58:13.079 --> 58:16.079
You can't possibly
be that naive.

58:16.162 --> 58:19.579
There are 16 RBMK reactors

58:19.663 --> 58:22.454
running in the Soviet Union
right now.

58:22.538 --> 58:24.496
We have to fix them.

58:24.579 --> 58:27.287
The only way to do that
is to go public,

58:27.371 --> 58:29.371
force the Central Committee
to take action.

58:29.454 --> 58:32.454
What you're proposing is that
Legasov humiliate a nation

58:32.538 --> 58:35.538
that is obsessed with
not being humiliated.

58:35.621 --> 58:38.079
We can make a deal
with the KGB.

58:38.162 --> 58:40.246
You'll leave this information
out in Vienna,

58:40.329 --> 58:43.454
and they quietly let us fix
the remaining reactors.

58:43.538 --> 58:45.871
A deal with the KGB?

58:45.955 --> 58:47.663
And I'm "naive."

58:48.913 --> 58:52.371
Shcherbina:
They'll go after your family,
they'll go after your friends.

58:52.454 --> 58:55.287
Khomyuk:
You have a chance to talk
to the world, Valery.

58:55.371 --> 58:57.246
If that chance was mine--

58:57.329 --> 58:58.996
But it isn't, is it?

59:00.246 --> 59:03.371
I've know braver souls
than you, Khomyuk.

59:03.454 --> 59:05.621
Men who had their moment
and did nothing.

59:05.705 --> 59:09.830
Because when it's your life and
the lives of everyone you love,

59:09.913 --> 59:12.538
your moral conviction
doesn't mean anything.

59:12.621 --> 59:14.746
It leaves you.

59:14.830 --> 59:19.371
And all you want at that moment
is not to be shot.

59:23.413 --> 59:25.788
Do you know the name
Vasily Ignatenko?

59:25.871 --> 59:27.413
No.

59:28.746 --> 59:31.496
He was a fireman.

59:31.579 --> 59:34.663
He died two weeks
after the accident.

59:34.746 --> 59:37.621
I've been looking in
on his widow.

59:37.705 --> 59:39.496
She gave birth.

59:39.579 --> 59:40.996
A girl.

59:41.079 --> 59:43.371
The baby lived
for four hours.

59:44.287 --> 59:46.413
They said the radiation
would have killed the mother,

59:46.496 --> 59:49.162
but the baby
absorbed it instead.

59:49.246 --> 59:50.663
Her baby.

59:52.246 --> 59:53.788
We live in a country

59:53.871 --> 59:56.579
where children have to die
to save their mothers.

59:57.830 --> 59:59.955
To hell with your deal.

01:00:01.955 --> 01:00:04.287
And to hell with our lives.

01:00:05.871 --> 01:00:08.121
Someone has to start
telling the truth.

01:00:22.287 --> 01:00:24.663
Tarakanov:
Congratulations, comrades.

01:00:24.746 --> 01:00:28.287
You are the last of 3,828 men.

01:00:28.371 --> 01:00:31.037
You have performed
your duties perfectly.

01:00:31.121 --> 01:00:33.538
I wish you good health
and long life.

01:00:33.621 --> 01:00:36.496
All of you are awarded
a bonus of 800 rubles.

01:00:36.579 --> 01:00:38.329
-Thank you.
-I serve the Soviet Union.

01:00:38.413 --> 01:00:40.246
-Thank you.
-I serve the Soviet Union.

01:00:40.329 --> 01:00:41.996
-Thank you.
-I serve the Soviet Union.

01:00:42.079 --> 01:00:43.830
-Thank you.
-I serve the Soviet Union.

01:00:43.913 --> 01:00:45.830
-Thank you.
-I serve the Soviet Union.

01:00:45.913 --> 01:00:47.579
-Thank you.
-I serve the Soviet Union.

01:00:47.663 --> 01:00:49.162
-Thank you.
-I serve the Soviet Union.

01:00:49.246 --> 01:00:50.496
-Thank you.
-I serve the Soviet Union.

01:00:50.579 --> 01:00:52.746
-Thank you.
-I serve the Soviet Union.

01:01:26.705 --> 01:01:28.830
(infants crying)

01:04:51.454 --> 01:04:53.037
JUDGE: This session of court
is now open.

01:04:54.079 --> 01:04:56.162
The state calls Comrade Khomyuk.

01:04:57.079 --> 01:04:58.746
ULANA KHOMYUK: To understand
what happened that night,

01:04:58.830 --> 01:05:01.121
we have to go back
to the first critical moment.

01:05:01.913 --> 01:05:03.454
The time is 28 past midnight.

01:05:06.746 --> 01:05:09.413
At the trial,
you're going to tell the truth.

01:05:09.788 --> 01:05:11.579
MAN: 1:22 a.m.

01:05:11.996 --> 01:05:13.621
Once it's over,
we will have our villains.

01:05:14.121 --> 01:05:16.705
We will have our hero.
We will have our truth.

01:05:17.246 --> 01:05:19.788
MAN: 1:23 and 35 seconds.

01:05:19.996 --> 01:05:21.996
JUDGE: Comrade Boris Shcherbina.

01:05:22.538 --> 01:05:25.454
It began with... a safety test.

01:05:25.705 --> 01:05:27.454
-MAN: 1:23:42.
-(ALARMS BEEP)

01:05:28.287 --> 01:05:31.705
KHOMYUK: They died rescuing
each other. Putting out fires.

01:05:32.579 --> 01:05:33.746
-Tending to the wounded.
-(BEEPING CONTINUES)

01:05:33.955 --> 01:05:35.538
MAN: 1:23:45.

01:05:35.621 --> 01:05:37.454
KHOMYUK:
When your testimony arrives,

01:05:38.371 --> 01:05:39.579
insist on reform.

01:05:39.996 --> 01:05:41.746
-I've already given my life.
-(BEEPING ACCELERATES)

01:05:42.204 --> 01:05:44.162
-Isn't that enough?
-(BEEPING ENDS)

01:05:44.371 --> 01:05:46.454
JUDGE:
The state calls Comrade Legasov.
